THE ROLE:&nbsp;

You will be the owner of deal creation and the first line of analysis for deal performance. You’ll manage a portfolio of accounts, track results using DSP reporting data, and spot scaling or delivery issues early. You’ll work closely with Customer Success &amp; Sales

Key Responsibilities &nbsp;

• Own deal creation: Receive requests and build all deals accurately and on time. &nbsp;

• Account management and reporting: Manage assigned accounts and build Excel tracking documents for your campaigns.&nbsp; &nbsp;

• Optimization tracking: Log every deal optimization and measure its impact on performance. &nbsp;

• Performance monitoring: Flag performance issues and significant spend drops to the Manager for troubleshooting. &nbsp;

• Weekly updates: Deliver weekly account updates to the Customer Success Team. &nbsp;

• Deal health analysis: Review deal health across SSPs using bid request data and troubleshooting tools. Give clear insights on scaling challenges before escalating to the Manager. &nbsp;

• Ticket management: Maintain Jira tickets, keep statuses accurate and current, and respond to raised questions. &nbsp;

• Cross-team partnership: Work with Customer Success and Sales to resolve troubleshooting questions and account issues. &nbsp;

&nbsp;

Required Qualifications &nbsp;

• Excel skills: PivotTables, SUM/SUMIFS, VLOOKUP, Name Manager, and the ability to review large datasets quickly and accurately. &nbsp;

• Strong attention to detail and a structured, organized working style. &nbsp;

• Fluent in English, both spoken and written, for daily work with US-based teams &nbsp;

• Clear written communication, especially for status updates and escalations. &nbsp;

• Ability to prioritize across multiple accounts and deadlines. &nbsp;

&nbsp;

Preferred Qualifications &nbsp;

• 1 to 3 years in programmatic advertising, ad operations, or deal/account support. &nbsp;

• Familiarity with DSPs, SSPs, PMP/deal IDs, and bid request troubleshooting. &nbsp;

• Experience with Jira or a similar ticketing system. &nbsp;

• College degree (or equivalent experience) in Marketing. &nbsp;

&nbsp;

What Success Looks Like &nbsp;

• Deals are created accurately and on time. &nbsp;

• Optimizations are logged, and their impact is clearly documented. &nbsp;

• Tracking documents for accounts are all made &nbsp;

• Spend drops and performance issues are flagged early, with context. &nbsp;

• Escalations arrive with analysis, not just a problem statement. &nbsp;

• Jira tickets are always current. &nbsp;

&nbsp;

