For an International Institution in Geneva, we are urgently looking for a Full remote Senior Business Analyst for an external-facing web development project.

Candidates need to be fluent in English. This positions is long-term. Candidates need to be based in Europe. Work permit is not provided.

Tasks and responsibilities:

Develop a business analysis workplan for the duration of the project;

Establish appropriate business analysis methodology and business analysis documentation templates for ODP NextGen (population data management, data visualization, document repository, administrative functions, overall functionality of the Portal);

Lead use case documentation and requirements analysis;

Conduct a detailed review and define essential/prioritized requirements for the new version of the system, including feedback from support colleagues and field users;

Conduct interviews with relevant staff at headquarters, regional bureaus, and field to identify requirements and gather feedback;

Participate in technology selection, provide support for the fit/gap analysis;

Draft detailed functional specifications for prioritized requirements in close collaboration with focal points;

Provide content on progress for project communications;

Lead User Acceptance Testing, generate test scripts and scenarios;

Profile:

Bachelor or Master degree;

+8 years of Business Analyst experience;

Experience working as the primary Senior Business Analyst;

+3 years of experience working with global-scale, external-facing web development projects;

Previous experience working as a business analyst on projects migrating production systems to a new technology stack (e.g., requirements documentation, systems configuration, test documentation/execution, issue identification and resolution);

Previous experience working with headless/low-code/no-code technologies;

Familiar with formal I.T. project management best practices (PRINCE2, PMBOK) and experience with Agile methodologies;

Fluent in English;

Interested: Please send your resume

